@* A real Blazor component that reads a BROWSER API — and still knows nothing about Rask.

   This is the half of Rask.Blazor that did not work before #956. The component injects
   Microsoft's own IJSRuntime, which on a Rask host resolves to Rask's implementation, and calls it
   from OnAfterRenderAsync — a hook StaticHtmlRenderer never fires and Rask now drives.

   Two things are being proved at once, which is why this component exists rather than a unit test:
   [Inject] actually delivers a service (it silently delivered null before), and the identifier it
   calls — __raskApi.matchMedia — is Rask's shared browser layer, the same TypeScript module a
   TypeScript front end imports as browser/mediaQuery.

   Styled inline for the same reason as PriceTicker.razor: Tailwind scans the app's directory, not
   this library's. *@

@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@inject IJSRuntime Js

<div data-testid="viewport-probe"
     style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.75rem;align-items:center;padding:.75rem 1rem;
            border:1px solid #cbd5e1;border-radius:.5rem;font-family:system-ui,sans-serif">

    <strong>Colour scheme</strong>

    @* "…" until the hook has run, so the E2E can tell "never ran" from "ran and said light". *@
    <span data-testid="probe-scheme" style="font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums">@_scheme</span>
</div>

@code {
    private string _scheme = "…";

    /// <summary>
    ///     Runs once, after the island's first paint. On the Server host the call escalates the page to
    ///     a live session through Rask's ordinary path, so the answer arrives over the socket that is
    ///     already open — no circuit, no blazor.web.js.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    ///     Do NOT call StateHasChanged from here unconditionally. It is Blazor's own documented trap —
    ///     the hook feeds the render that fires it — and hosted in an island it recurses through the
    ///     renderer. Guarding on firstRender, as here, is the shape that is safe.
    /// </remarks>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!firstRender)
        {
            return;
        }

        var dark = await Js.InvokeAsync<bool>("__raskApi.matchMedia", "(prefers-color-scheme: dark)");
        _scheme = dark ? "dark" : "light";
        StateHasChanged();
    }
}
